ADR-0049 open work step 3 cleared with measurement 0010, so the family the pin
has held since 2026-08-28 moves. 28 rows -> net_listen, in four languages:

  go       net/http.{ListenAndServe,ListenAndServeTLS,Serve}, gin Run/RunTLS,
           echo Start/StartTLS, fiber Listen/ListenTLS, grpc Server.Serve
  python   {HTTPServer,TCPServer,SimpleXMLRPCServer}.{serve_forever,
           handle_request}, asyncio.{start_server,start_unix_server},
           flask.Flask.run, uvicorn.run, aiohttp.web.run_app
  haskell  Warp.{run,runSettings,runTLS,runEnv}
  erlang   httpd.{start,start_service}, ssl.handshake

Each returns an error, a handle, or nothing; the request bytes reach a handler
the runtime invokes. That is ADR-0049 ruling 1's NO branch, and measurement
0010 adjudicated every live finding rooted in the family FALSE -- 2 on this
tree, 4 in measurement 0006.

RULING 3'S PROOF IS A RUN, PER LANGUAGE, NOT AN ARGUMENT. An idiomatic server
probe in each affected language, before and after:

  go       net_recv 2 [Accept, ListenAndServe]  ->  net_listen 1 + net_recv 1 [Accept]
  python   net_recv 2 [serve_forever, accept]   ->  net_listen 1 + net_recv 1 [accept]
  haskell  net_recv 3 [accept, recv, Warp.run]  ->  net_listen 1 + net_recv 2
  erlang   net_recv 3 [accept, recv, httpd]     ->  net_listen 1 + net_recv 2

Every language keeps a net_recv chain afterwards, so nothing was deleted where
the catalogue merely CLAIMED a counterpart -- the WI-lunav failure this rule
exists to catch.

TWO HOLDOUTS, DIFFERENT REASONS, ASSERTED SEPARATELY. JavaScript's whole
REACHABLE net_recv surface is {http,https,net}.createServer and Deno.listen;
what would survive -- WebSocket.onmessage and peers -- is INV-misup-unreachable,
so the move would relocate the receive to NOTHING. That is F2_EXEMPT's existing
reasoning, re-confirmed live by the same probe. Phoenix.Router is held because
0010 adjudicated NO findings for the route-registration shape, and absence of
findings is not evidence of harmlessness. One assertion covering both is how
the next retag takes the wrong one with it.

