FOUR RECALL-CORPUS FIXTURES RE-SOURCED, AND THAT IS THE FINDING-LEVEL HALF OF
RULING 3. test_taint_recall_corpus.py used asyncio.start_server and
net/http.ListenAndServe as its untrusted-input sources. They are re-pointed at
genuine transfers -- socket.socket.recv, and net.Conn.Read through a DECLARED
PARAMETER, the form that resolves (ln.Accept() after net.Listen does not,
WI-lalot) -- and every assertion holds unchanged. One needed more care: with a
socket.socket() constructor the repo's only call into the socket module is
unclassified, so the coverage gate withholds and the "source with no sink" test
would have passed its no-evidence line while failing its confirmed line. An
annotated parameter removes the unclassified call. A test that passes because
its source stopped existing is not a passing test.

